[{:db/id 17592186133889 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-22c40f40-e4e5-529d-a83f-3f46f140c8db" "question-36837fe3-6724-5929-9249-1bb3cf0a5e7f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-22c40f40-e4e5-529d-a83f-3f46f140c8db" :question/id #uuid "22c40f40-e4e5-529d-a83f-3f46f140c8db" :question/math-academy-id "q-105557" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F=xyz\\,i+{y}^{3}{x}^{2}\\,j+y{z}^{2}\\,k.$ \nFind $\\text{div}\\,F.$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the divergence of $F$ is the scalar field given by\n\n$$\n\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F=\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}F & =\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xyz)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{3}{x}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(y{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =yz+3{y}^{2}{x}^{2}+2yz \\\\  & =3yz+3{y}^{2}{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-69e44755-6b9a-5cca-b1ed-0c837e17c6d9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-69e44755-6b9a-5cca-b1ed-0c837e17c6d9" :answer-field/id #uuid "69e44755-6b9a-5cca-b1ed-0c837e17c6d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-88e03628-9e8e-5879-9ede-a96902f3797a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9a07bd93-8453-5012-b970-faf3a1a28f2f" "answer-88e03628-9e8e-5879-9ede-a96902f3797a" "answer-d674ed52-351d-5f4a-9c10-e0caa107251f" "answer-a8d3d9a8-1c50-5ad8-967c-67a2b8bdc976" "answer-13a914c9-ac5b-510b-8770-498ebbd342d6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a07bd93-8453-5012-b970-faf3a1a28f2f" :answer/id #uuid "9a07bd93-8453-5012-b970-faf3a1a28f2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3yz+2{y}^{3}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-88e03628-9e8e-5879-9ede-a96902f3797a" :answer/id #uuid "88e03628-9e8e-5879-9ede-a96902f3797a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3yz+3{y}^{2}{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d674ed52-351d-5f4a-9c10-e0caa107251f" :answer/id #uuid "d674ed52-351d-5f4a-9c10-e0caa107251f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4yz+2{y}^{3}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8d3d9a8-1c50-5ad8-967c-67a2b8bdc976" :answer/id #uuid "a8d3d9a8-1c50-5ad8-967c-67a2b8bdc976" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "xyz+3{y}^{2}{x}^{2}+2yz" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13a914c9-ac5b-510b-8770-498ebbd342d6" :answer/id #uuid "13a914c9-ac5b-510b-8770-498ebbd342d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "yz+3{y}^{2}{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186241080 :question/problem "![](images/11/11d38951b884f17616a61403d793322d0e2ea28910e806fe8f018251508352a1.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\nI. $∇\\cdot F=0$\n\nII. $∇\\cdot F>0$\n\nIII. $∇\\cdot F<0$\n\nIV. $F$ is solenoidal" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-36837fe3-6724-5929-9249-1bb3cf0a5e7f" :question/id #uuid "36837fe3-6724-5929-9249-1bb3cf0a5e7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-131175" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F={e}^{2x}\\,i-y{e}^{2x}\\,j-z{e}^{2x}\\,k.$ \nFind $∇\\cdot F.$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the divergence of $F$ is the scalar field given by\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot F=\\text{div}\\,F=\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{2x})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-y{e}^{2x})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(-z{e}^{2x}) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2x}-{e}^{2x}-{e}^{2x} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cbf3222d-f787-5312-b008-17567e5ae0c6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cbf3222d-f787-5312-b008-17567e5ae0c6" :answer-field/id #uuid "cbf3222d-f787-5312-b008-17567e5ae0c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-36f39977-9420-5792-a25e-40ed825c033a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-17ab80cc-c857-5dfb-9a3a-cfdfd3d6fc0b" "answer-36f39977-9420-5792-a25e-40ed825c033a" "answer-335bd84d-490e-5a69-979b-a11b772a9908" "answer-78e9e533-d5f7-5054-82d6-9d333edf1c19" "answer-af0cee1b-58b3-5b9b-a7e7-5c521761b047"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17ab80cc-c857-5dfb-9a3a-cfdfd3d6fc0b" :answer/id #uuid "17ab80cc-c857-5dfb-9a3a-cfdfd3d6fc0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36f39977-9420-5792-a25e-40ed825c033a" :answer/id #uuid "36f39977-9420-5792-a25e-40ed825c033a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-335bd84d-490e-5a69-979b-a11b772a9908" :answer/id #uuid "335bd84d-490e-5a69-979b-a11b772a9908" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78e9e533-d5f7-5054-82d6-9d333edf1c19" :answer/id #uuid "78e9e533-d5f7-5054-82d6-9d333edf1c19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2x}(1+y+z)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af0cee1b-58b3-5b9b-a7e7-5c521761b047" :answer/id #uuid "af0cee1b-58b3-5b9b-a7e7-5c521761b047" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2x}(2-y-z)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-b0b7ba59-d2e5-5c0e-aa1c-0c290b8b930c" :activity/id #uuid "b0b7ba59-d2e5-5c0e-aa1c-0c290b8b930c" :activity/title "The Divergence of a Vector Field" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049459 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-6a7d78a0-8d6d-590f-8d8a-84c35fdbd7e4" "step-0eb2dca7-e